id: brightened
name: Brightened
kind: conditions
# From Normal to Blinding is two Levels and from Pitch Black four, so four stacks is as far
# as it can ever take anybody. Past that it changes nothing. Darkened's mirror.
maxStacks: 4
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry raises a Square's Light Level and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# A Level up per stack. Read by `lightLevelOf`, which names no mark.
lightShift: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The light around you flares. Your Light Level is 1 higher per stack.
text: >
  Brightened: the Elemental (Light) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s)
  who take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver have their Light Level increased by 1 Level
  until the start of your next turn."

---

# Darkened's mirror, for the same reasons: there are no Squares, so the Level that goes up
# is the one on the character who took the Damage; it is a mark rather than a change to that
# field, because it runs out on the attacker's clock; and it stacks, one per hit, each with a
# clock of its own.
#
# A character both Darkened and Brightened is moved both ways: one of each is the Level
# they set. Nothing in the entry says one cancels the other, and adding them is what "reduced
# by 1" and "increased by 1" come to.
#
# No effects of its own: what a Light Level does is in that Level's own file.
